=== REASONING ===
New Redis writes use a JSON envelope that carries the raw value, a UTC timestamp, a source marker, and a legacy string encoding. The legacy string encoding lets existing raw-value methods continue returning the shapes older callers expect, while timestamp-aware reads can return signal.Value objects with the Redis timestamp.

Legacy scalar values are decoded by the timestamp-aware methods with Timestamp equal to the zero time. This intentionally does not fake freshness for old values that lack timestamps; consumers can distinguish unknown freshness from fresh live data.

Malformed JSON-shaped Redis values are surfaced as errors from timestamp-aware methods instead of being treated as fresh live state. Raw-value methods stay tolerant for backward compatibility.

Migration note: existing scalar Redis values are supported indefinitely and naturally replaced by timestamped values on the next telemetry write; no manual Redis migration is required.

